  "details": "Tried starting up the latest release of VRChat (2024.3.1) and as soon as it got beyond Easy Anti-Cheat everything froze because Avast decided to kill the executable, not because it suspected a virus but because it supposedly detected some generic thing.\n\nThis seems to be a trend; I've noticed this has happened several times with Avast and other virus scanners in the past. This time around though I'm wondering if that new video player popping up in the latest worlds which is downloading the YT-DLP executable has anything to do with it, as virus scanners also have a problem with that piece of software and maybe this has now carried over towards flagging the VRChat executable itself?",
